Paite Open Language Data: licence and rights

This repository contains original work and third-party text. Each part has its
own terms.

1. Original work: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)

   Applies to:
   - corrections.json
   - grammar_notes.md
   - the "verified_words", "verified_examples", and "verified_corrections"
     entries in paite_phrasebook.json
   - eval/ (the native-speaker benchmark)
   - glossary.json and CONTRIBUTORS.md
   - README.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, CITATION.cff, docs/, and this file
   - the selection, arrangement, and file formats of the collection

   You can copy, share, and adapt this work for any purpose, including
   commercial use, if you give credit to "Paite Open Language Data
   (github.com/khooptong-sudo/paite-open-language-data)" and state your changes.
   Full licence text: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode

2. Public domain

   - The English Bible text (World English Bible), including
     bible/world-english-bible/.
   - prompts/everyday_en.txt, dedicated to the public domain (CC0 1.0).

2a. Paite Daily translations: CC0 1.0 or CC BY 4.0, line by line

   Every file in community/ holds translations sent through Paite Daily
   (paite.lamkalabs.com) and verified by reviewers. Each line has a
   "licence" field, and that field is the licence of that line:

   - "CC0-1.0": answers sent before 21 October 2026, 18:47 UTC. The form
     then said the translations were given to everyone as public domain, so
     these lines carry no conditions:
     https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/
   - "CC-BY-4.0": answers sent from then on. The form says the translations
     are free to use with credit. Credit "Paite Daily, Lamka Labs" and,
     where the line names one, its contributor:
     https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

   New translations are CC BY 4.0.

2b. Voice recordings: CC BY 4.0

   - Every file in audio/. Speakers on Paite Daily read verified Paite lines
     aloud. Before recording, each speaker ticked: "I agree my voice reading
     this line is published under CC BY 4.0, with my name if I gave one." A
     reviewer accepted every clip before it was published. Credit "Paite
     Daily, Lamka Labs" and the speaker named in audio/recordings.jsonl:
     https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
   - A clip is removed from audio/ if its review is undone. Past versions stay
     in the git history.

2c. Code: MIT OR Apache-2.0

   - Every file in scripts/ and .github/. You may use the code under either
     the MIT licence (scripts/LICENSE-MIT) or the Apache License 2.0
     (scripts/LICENSE-APACHE), at your choice.

3. Used with permission

   - The Paite Bible text in bible/laisiangthou/ and the Bible rows in
     training/. Source: the Laisiangthou app (v5.0.2) by John Samte
     (https://github.com/johnsamte), who gave permission for its use in this
     repository. Credit John Samte when you use this text. Ask him before any
     commercial use.

4. Third-party text: NOT licensed by this repository

   - Paite Bible text in bible/legacy-etabetapi/ (collected from
     etabetapi.com). Copyright of the original Paite Bible publisher.
   - Dictionary data in dictionary/Paite+English+Dictionary_1_1_4_apkcombo_com.json
     and the "dictionary" key of paite_phrasebook.json. Copyright of the
     author of the "Paite English Dictionary" Android app.
   - Hymn lyrics and snippets in songs/Kristian+Labu_1_4_53_apkcombo_com.json,
     songs/Biakna+Labupi_1_0_0_apkcombo_com.json, and the "song_titles" key of
     paite_phrasebook.json. Copyright of the hymn authors, translators, and
     app publishers.

   This text is included for non-commercial research, education, and language
   preservation. The maintainer does not claim ownership of it and grants no
   rights to it. You are responsible for your own use of it.

   Rights holders: to request removal or a change of credit, open an issue at
   https://github.com/khooptong-sudo/paite-open-language-data/issues

5. Mixed files

   - training/ and paite_phrasebook.json combine the parts above. In
     training/, the "source" field of each row names its part; for rows with
     "source": "community", the line in community/ with the same "id" (before
     any ":1", ":2" suffix) gives its licence.

THE DATA IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED,
INCLUDING THE WARRANTIES OF ACCURACY AND FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE.
